<title>JAPAN: Nippon Mining ups indium price by 4,000 yen per kg.</title>
<headline>Nippon Mining ups indium price by 4,000 yen per kg.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Mining and Metals Co said on Friday it had raised its selling price for indium ingots by 4,000 yen to 33,000 yen per kg for large orders and to 38,000 yen per kg for small orders for 99.99 percent pure metal, effective with March 3 shipments.</p>
<p>The company cited supply tightness and rising prices overseas among the reasons for the price hike, which followed a 3,000 yen price increase on January 28.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 6179</p>
</text>
